<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak import deposits to be held in c.bank-FinMin.</title>
<headline>Slovak import deposits to be held in c.bank-FinMin.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deposits for the recently adopted Slovak import deposit scheme will be held by the central bank through the state-run Konsolidacna Banka s.p.u., the Finance Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The government ruled that funds (from import deposits) will be channelled from commercial banks to Konsolidacna Banka which will then deposit them on its account in the National Bank of Slovakia (NBS),&quot; Finance Ministry Spokesman Jozef Mach told Reuters after a regular government meeting.</p>
</text>
